      "task_id": "closure2-state-machine-refactor",
      "family": "N1",
      "title": "Coupled state machine refactor",
      "goal": "The order lifecycle state machine in `lifecycle/state.py` must grow two terminal states (`rejected`, `cancelled`) and the events that reach them, and every caller must be moved onto the same table. Approvals, shipping and the audit trail all read the same `STATES` mapping, so the machine and its callers are one change: a caller that hard-codes a transition the table does not contain is a defect, and an illegal transition must be rejected rather than raising `KeyError`.",
